# Scratch.
#
# BEFORE WIDENING ANY PATTERN HERE, READ THIS (#473, and the battle-builder design §5a).
# `scenarios/` is a *committed* library of JSON — versioned, diffable, quotable in an
# issue, reviewable in a PR, readable by CI — and nothing in this file may swallow it.
# #469 is widening the save-file rule below to the `--save=<path>` family, and its own
# criteria correctly call for an **unanchored** pattern, since saves land in `client/`
# rather than at the root. Unanchored is right for saves and one careless `*.json` away
# from making the whole scenario library invisible with `git status` clean — which is
# worse than losing it outright, because tests/SRDCombat.Game.Tests/ScenarioLibraryTests
# keeps passing on the files already in the index while every new scenario silently fails
# to arrive.
#
# The check, run after any change here: `git check-ignore -v scenarios/*.json` must print
# nothing and exit 1. It does today.
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.old

# Save files (#469): the Godot client's --save=<path> writes wherever it is asked to
# (client/README.md), not just the default srdcombat-save.json, and it lands in
# whatever directory Godot was launched from (client/, for client work) rather than
# the repo root — so this is deliberately unanchored, unlike the tracked JSON below it
# is not meant to shadow. Kept narrow to the save family on purpose (srdcombat-save*,
# plus the .bak/.old rotation the atomic-write path produces, already covered above):
# a broader *.json rule would also hide data/srd's committed content and the
# scenarios/ directory #473 is landing, which needs to stay visible in `git status`.
srdcombat-save*.json

# Agent worktrees, scratch output, and temp working dirs.
#
# `.claude/worktrees/` reached 3.7 GB across nine stale agent checkouts, untracked
# and unignored. The cost was not disk: every repo-wide agent search saw ten copies
# of the tree (`find . -name Encounter.cs` returned 10 hits; a grep for
# `EndBrokenGrapples` matched 9 files), so each search paid ~10x the tokens and could
# read a stale copy as if it were `src/`. The search tools honour .gitignore, so
# ignoring these directories is what actually restores single-copy search results.
#
# Prefer creating agent worktrees OUTSIDE the repository (the session scratchpad) so
# a nested checkout never lands in the working tree at all; these entries are the
# backstop for when one does.
.claude/worktrees/
output/
tmp/

# Test output (scripts/status.sh reads the trx from here)
TestResults/
